/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=()
  # Two analytics beacons, and each needs naming twice — once in `script-src`
  # for the tag that loads, once in `connect-src` for the host it reports to,
  # because they are different hosts in both cases and `connect-src 'self'`
  # covers neither. Miss either half and the failure is quiet in the worst way:
  # the site looks perfectly fine, every page load logs a console violation
  # nobody is watching, and the dashboard just shows no traffic.
  #
  #   Cloudflare Web Analytics — injected at the edge rather than by the app,
  #   so it appears in no source file here. static.cloudflareinsights.com
  #   serves it, cloudflareinsights.com receives it. Page views and web vitals.
  #
  #   Umami — the tag in `nuxt.config.ts`, carrying the custom events from
  #   `composables/track.ts`. This is the one that answers whether anyone
  #   downloads the CV, and it takes *three* hosts rather than the two the
  #   sentence above would suggest: cloud.umami.is serves the tag, and Umami
  #   Cloud ingests on gateway.umami.is, which appears nowhere in the snippet
  #   they hand you. Naming only cloud.umami.is is the exact failure this
  #   comment warns about — measured on the live site 2026-08-19, the script
  #   loaded 200, `window.umami` was present, and every POST to
  #   gateway.umami.is/api/send was refused by this header.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://cloud.umami.is; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com https://cloud.umami.is https://gateway.umami.is; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Hashed build assets are immutable — safe to cache forever.
/_nuxt/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
